meta {
  name: Evaluation (LLM-as-Judge)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "{{budgetModel}}",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "system",
        "content": "You are a judge. Score the answer's accuracy 1–5."
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Question: Which headphones have the best noise cancellation under $300?\nAnswer: The Sony WH-1000XM5 offers 30-hour battery with top-rated noise cancellation at $299."
      }
    ],
    "max_tokens": 64
  }
}

docs {
  LLM-as-Judge evaluation call: uses the budget model to score a generated
  answer for quality without the `X-Rag-Operation` header.

  The classifier detects evaluation from the system prompt keywords "judge" and
  "score", so cost is recorded under the `evaluation` bucket. You can also pass
  `X-Rag-Operation: evaluation` explicitly to force the tag.

  This pattern is common for nightly quality-drift detection: run a batch of
  (question, answer) pairs through the judge and alert when the average score
  drops.
}
